    "name": "Capace Hotel Gangnam",
    "detail": "This is my first time to go to Seoul and here's some points I'd like to recommend: 1. Good problem solving： Although the staff in the front desk cannot speak in English, they assisted me with another staff who can speak in Chinese. And they assist me to solve the logement pronblem cuz I'm too early for check-in and it's cold outside. 2. Good location： It's easy to reach Capace Hotel by walking after taking metro from the nearest station. Taking the shuttle bus to belle-essence station and walk only 5 mins to find Capace. 3. Good service： Actually not the best service from the hotels I've stay before in other countries. But daily cleaness is good and they won't disturb you if you stay in hotel all day. 4. Conveneint to stores nearby： Right in front the hill by hotel, there's a cafeteria and convenient store. Starbucks and even supermarkets are along the road of the hotel. Most importantly, the environment is quiet and comfortable. I will stay again next time!",
